    "L6_top_supported_1": "Crime & Social Order — Key Statistics (1910)\n\n| Metric | Value | Source |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Property Crime (% of commitments) | 60–70% | State/Federal Prisons |\n| Offenses Against the Person (% of commitments) | 13–24% | State/Federal Prisons |\n| Robbery (% of commitments) | ~9% | State/Federal Prisons |\n| Total Lynchings (1900–1919) | ~1,500 | NAACP / Academic |\n| Black Victims (% of Total Lynchings) | ~72% | NAACP / Academic |\n\nPrisoner-commitment data shows a remarkably consistent crime distribution: property offenses accounted for 60 to 70 percent of commitments; offenses against the person (homicide, assault, rape) accounted for 13 to 24 percent.",
